{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Some people have had a buffer but that will begin to erode as interest rates get higher, and the Reserve Bank has made it pretty clear, and the private banks are expecting this as well that Australians need to brace for more interest rate rises. We have got this inflation problem \u8211  it will get worse before it gets better, but it will get better, it will moderate next year. }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 One of the things I want to do in the ministerial statement that I will deliver next Thursday, the 28th, and the parliament is to talk about the things we have working for us \u8211  the low unemployment rate for example but also that things working against us, and I think the most confronting aspect of the ministerial statement will be our expectations for inflation, and also the impact of rising interest rates on economic growth.}
