\ulnone\cf2 Jim Chalmers says he goes into the RBA review with a \u8220 genuinely open mind\u8221 :}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I go into this review with an open mind, genuinely an open mind, about the best combination of institutional arrangements for the Reserve Bank so that we have the world\u8217 s best bank relying on adopting world\u8217 s best practice, and focusing on the future.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I want this to be a forward-looking overview, all about the best combination of arrangements into the future.  I don\u8217 t want it to be an exercise in hot shots or second guessing, I don\u8217 t want it to be exclusively focused on a backward-looking blame-shifting exercise. }
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I want to genuinely see it being about how we have the world\u8217 s best central bank into the future, and how do we make sure that the institutional and other arrangements are set up as well as they can be to ensure that the right decisions, sometimes difficult decisions, are taken in the future in the interest of Australians and their economy.}
